WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.040
- What's in a name?

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:03.210
That which we call a
rose by any other name

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:04.420
would smell as sweet.

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.920
Well, Shakespeare, turns
out that ain't true,

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.978
especially when it comes to baby names.

00:00:08.978 --> 00:00:11.410
I don't care how cute your baby is,

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:14.870
the pressure is on for
the perfect baby name.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:18.340
And believe me, when I
say everybody you know

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.790
has an opinion on your baby's name.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:22.980
Heaven forbid you wanna
name your baby Brad

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.440
but your sister-in-law
once dated a kid named Brad

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.280
who had rancid cheese breath.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:30.970
I mean, do you really
want that association?

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:35.020
Do you want baby Brad, the
rancid cheese breath baby?

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:36.140
I don't think so.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.130
Believe me when I say finding

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:41.150
the perfect baby name is not easy.

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:43.250
Luckily, through trial and error,

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.860
and some pretty unique techniques,

00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:50.250
I was able to find the perfect baby name.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.920
And today I'm feeling nice,

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.870
so I'm gonna let you in on that secret.

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.800
This is how you find
the perfect baby name.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.140
Whether you're looking
for a new name for a baby

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:01.320
or yourself, you gotta start with a list.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.950
But where do you find
names to put on the list?

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:05.930
Well, you can use your memory.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:07.980
You can look at objects around you.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:11.030
Crib, ice cream. Those could be names.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:13.240
Maybe not good names,
but they could be names.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:14.520
The most common places to look

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:16.140
are books with baby names.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.120
There's a lot of websites, listicles.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.770
The Social Security Administration

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.200
has a bunch of baby names.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.438
Those are all easy places
to find ideas for names.

00:01:24.438 --> 00:01:27.070
If you're really interested
in a family name,

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:31.410
you can look old family
trees or ancestry.com

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.200
to see if there's anything up there

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.680
that you hadn't seen before.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.750
This is something that
my partner and I did.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:37.764
There were some gems.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:40.382
In his family tree, the name Olga came up.

00:01:40.382 --> 00:01:42.916
And in mine, the name Capitola.

00:01:42.916 --> 00:01:45.913
Now we did not end up
going with those names,

00:01:45.913 --> 00:01:48.000
so those names are free for
the taking, you're welcome.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.030
There are also a lot of different apps

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:52.550
you can use that can help you find a name

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:54.430
that you and your partner can agree on.

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:55.950
You basically both download the app.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.560
You swipe right or left, whether
you like the name or not,

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:01.190
and the names that you both
like will show up on a list.

00:02:01.190 --> 00:02:02.670
So you don't even have to talk

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:04.260
to your partner to find a baby name.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:06.030
And isn't that the way it should be?

00:02:06.030 --> 00:02:08.320
You can also ask social media.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:11.210
In my case, I asked YouTube commenters

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:13.130
and I got some pretty creative ones.

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:15.230
My also got a lotta,

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:16.063
you know what?

00:02:16.063 --> 00:02:17.740
They didn't have my baby's
best interest at heart,

00:02:17.740 --> 00:02:18.720
let's just say that.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.130
But say, you've checked those places

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:22.440
and you're still like, "Oh,
I'm not finding anything."

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:25.830
There are some weirder
places you can look.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.260
There's the obituary.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:29.550
And I know that sounds dark,

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:32.750
but old time-y names are
making a comeback now,

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:35.260
so you would actually be very on trend.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:36.880
And if you're more adventurous,

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.860
you can actually go to a cemetery.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.820
I know, again, that sounds very dark,

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:44.590
but my sister, her name
actually comes from my parents

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:49.350
going to a family grave
site and finding her name.

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:50.613
Okay, so here's the cemetery.

00:02:50.613 --> 00:02:52.378
There's a lot of different names.

00:02:52.378 --> 00:02:54.090
We're gonna take a look.

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:56.729
What do you think of the name Gavlin?

00:02:56.729 --> 00:02:57.900
- [Man] Ursula.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.766
I think Ursula is a cool name.

00:02:59.766 --> 00:03:01.270
Ciaran Arthur.

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:02.640
- And finally, when you're making a list,

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.890
you might wanna honor
your cultural heritage.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:06.930
And there's a lot of different
sites you can look at,

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:09.580
but you can also just
go to the Wikipedia page

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:13.360
of your hometown and see
who famous is from there.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:16.807
Alex Azar, Frank Perdue,
if you're into chickens.

00:03:16.807 --> 00:03:19.290
Or like I said, that
could be a bit of a bust.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:20.480
Just an idea.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.260
Okay, so now you have your list of names.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:23.690
Congrats, okay.

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:28.190
You're halfway there, but now
the real hard work begins.

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:30.720
How do you pick the name from this list?

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:32.740
You probably want something that's unique,

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:34.450
but not too unique.

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:36.010
There's a website called datayze

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:38.306
that is a baby name uniqueness analyzer.

00:03:38.306 --> 00:03:41.540
It uses information from the
Social Security Administration

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:45.380
and will tell you what the
chance your particular baby name

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:47.810
has of being in the
same kindergarten class

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:48.860
with somebody of that name.

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.260
That could be important to you.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:51.700
I had a pretty common name

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:55.000
and so I was looking for a
name that was not as common.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.070
I do not like it when
someone else has my name

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:00.910
and my sister-in-law has my name.

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:02.400
We are both Sarah Burton.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.840
Whether or not you wanna
find something super unique,

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:07.650
it's useful because popular baby names

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:09.020
have been trending down.

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:11.330
And by that, I mean a
smaller percentage of babies

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:13.330
are given one of the top 10 names

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:17.110
than would have happened
10, 20, 30 years ago.

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:18.860
They're just more names to pick from.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:20.600
And they're more names being used.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:22.410
So my baby's already gonna have

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.980
a pretty unpronounceable last name.

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:28.440
So it was important to me
that their unique first name

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.310
was still largely phonetic,

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:32.470
that it could be pronounced pretty easy.

00:04:32.470 --> 00:04:33.890
We have a list of names.

00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:36.010
Yeah, some of them were from cemetery

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:38.740
and some of them were from the name app,

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:39.940
stuff we both liked.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.520
And I think we do have a front runner

00:04:41.520 --> 00:04:45.130
that actually showed up at
both places, creepily enough.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:47.366
But it's a name with a
lot of different spellings

00:04:47.366 --> 00:04:50.260
and so we have to figure that out.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:51.350
It never ends.

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:52.680
Another thing you'll have to deal with

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:56.490
is how to spell the name,
which can honestly be

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:59.720
as controversial as the name itself.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:01.470
If you're between a few spellings,

00:05:01.470 --> 00:05:03.210
this is a good rule of thumb.

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:04.790
Does this name look like

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:06.770
it came out of the Canterbury Tales?

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:08.650
Does it look Old English?

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:10.800
Are there Y's all over the place?

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:14.820
It's 2021, not 1365.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:16.400
Finally, probably the biggest way

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:19.130
to narrow down the names is to find out

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:21.770
what your baby's sex at birth will be.

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:23.670
Hi, my name's Sarah Burton

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.946
and I just missed a
call about test results.

00:05:25.946 --> 00:05:29.783
- [Doctor] You are having a baby boy.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.400
- I mean, for me, it
helped me stop referring

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.560
to my baby as an it, which was nice.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:38.080
Although this probably isn't
as effective as it used to be

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:40.280
because unisex and gender neutral names

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:41.640
are very in right now.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:44.860
So you think you've zeroed
in on a particular name?

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:47.580
Now this is where stuff
gets really tricky.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.730
It's the hardest part.

00:05:48.730 --> 00:05:50.600
Telling other people the baby's name.

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.180
Telling other people the
name is the truest test

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:55.390
of whether your baby name sucks.

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:56.365
You can avoid this step

00:05:56.365 --> 00:05:59.130
by not telling anybody the baby's name

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:00.480
until the baby is born.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:02.739
What, are people gonna look
at this cute little baby

00:06:02.739 --> 00:06:05.240
and tell the baby that the name sucks?

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.277
Are they gonna look at
baby Brad and be like,

00:06:07.277 --> 00:06:11.030
"Oh Brad, you have a
rancid cheese baby name,

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:12.390
you stupid, baby"?

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:13.660
No, they're not gonna do that.

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:15.690
You wouldn't say that to a baby.

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:18.660
You would say that to
the parents of the baby.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:19.940
So here's what you should do.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:22.760
You wanna start slow, introduce the name,

00:06:22.760 --> 00:06:24.690
give them the background.

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:28.750
How long, how hard it was
for you to get to that name.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:30.790
They're not gonna jump
on you when they know

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.190
you've been really struggling
with this decision.

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:35.549
All right, so I know I
talked big game up top

00:06:35.549 --> 00:06:37.770
about how to find the perfect baby name.

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:40.430
I know that that's the
whole concept of this video.

00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:43.410
There really isn't just
one perfect baby name.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:45.040
There's a lot of perfect baby names

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:47.080
and they're all different for each person.

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:49.050
There are also a lot of bad baby names

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:50.540
and you need to be aware of those.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:52.020
I'll put them in a list at the end,

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:53.440
just don't pick any of those.

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:56.900
We actually ended up picking
a name based on that app.

00:06:56.900 --> 00:07:00.020
It was one that we both swiped right on

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.350
and we kept coming back to it.

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:02.700
We have a list of names.

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:04.825
Yeah, some of them were from the cemetery

00:07:04.825 --> 00:07:07.590
and some of them were from the name app.

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:09.170
And I think we do have a front runner

00:07:09.170 --> 00:07:11.430
that actually showed up at both places.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:13.770
It's also a name you can find
in several different cultures,

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:15.390
so it's largely pronounceable.

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:17.590
It's not in the top 100 baby names,

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:20.430
but it is in the top 500 baby names.

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:23.720
Now, my husband does want to wait for us

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:26.920
to tell everyone the name
until the baby is born,

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:29.070
so you can't be mean to the baby face.

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:31.150
But, you know, I'm making this video,

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:32.610
so I'm obviously gonna tell you.

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:37.217
The baby's name is going to
be (bleep) Burton Hromchak.

00:07:39.499 --> 00:07:41.686
(music stops abruptly)

00:07:41.686 --> 00:07:44.470
(Beep) Burton Hromchak.

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:47.120
The baby's name is (beep),
the baby's name is (beep).

00:07:49.644 --> 00:07:52.320
How the hell did he learn to bleep?

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:55.077
That motherf--
(upbeat music)

